ater he watches two women on a hill above a pond in the evening sun, is struck by the beauty of their colors, and says nothing from his own inexperience. When one woman, who is a nurse, glances at him closely, he feels a sudden fear and is shaken by her look. At a garden where he has been asked to sweep fallen cherry leaves, he sits idle until Satomi Mineko appears, and he admits to her that he was only there to sweep."}]}
