{"entries":[{"name":"ジョバンニ","reading":"じょばんに","category":"character","keys":["ジョバンニ","ジョバンニさん"],"content":"Giovanni is a schoolboy in class at the afternoon lesson. When the teacher asks about the Milky Way, he raises his hand but cannot answer clearly, and he blushes as Zanelli laughs at him. He remembers reading about the stars with Campanella at Campanella's house, and he feels sad because he has been tired from hard work, less lively at school, and talking less with his friends. After school he hurries home to his mother, who is ill and resting, and brings her sugar cubes for her milk. He eats tomato and bread, and says he believes his father will return soon because a newspaper reported good fishing in the north. He still delivers newspapers to the Campanella house every morning. On the night of the Milky Way festival he carries warm milk bottles and goes out with Campanella and their friends, and later hears that a child has fallen into the river. He runs to the river and finds Maruso, who tells him that Campanella jumped in after Zanelli and has not been found."},{"name":"カムパネルラ","reading":"かむぱねるら","category":"character","keys":["カムパネルラ","カムパネルラさん"],"content":"Campanella is a schoolboy in Giovanni's class who readily raises his hand to answer the teacher's question about the Milky Way. When called on, he stands but cannot answer. He is Giovanni's close friend, and the two once looked at a large book about the Milky Way together in the study of Campanella's father, a doctor. Giovanni suspects Campanella did not answer right away out of kindness, to spare Giovanni's feelings. Campanella never teases Giovanni about his father's broken promise of a sea otter jacket, and looks sorry for him when others do. His house once had a toy train running on an alcohol lamp, and Giovanni often stopped there on his way home from school. On the festival night he goes to float lanterns on the river with Giovanni, and when Zanelli falls into the water, Campanella jumps in and pushes Zanelli toward the boat. Afterward he cannot be found, and the people searching the river include his father."},{"name":"ザネリ","reading":"ざねり","category":"character","keys":["ザネリ"],"content":"Zanelli is a classmate who sits in the front seat. When Giovanni cannot answer the teacher's question, Zanelli turns around and smiles at him, which makes Giovanni embarrassed. On the festival night he is in a boat pushing a lantern of kara-uri into the river when the boat rocks and he falls in. Campanella saves him by pushing him to the boat, where Katō holds him, and he is then taken home."},{"name":"ジョバンニの母","reading":"じょばんにのはは","category":"character","keys":["ジョバンニの母","お母さん","ジョバンニのお母さん"],"content":"Giovanni's mother is ill and rests in the front room of their small house, wrapped in a white cloth. She is glad when Giovanni brings home sugar cubes and asks whether the milk delivery came. She is gentle with Giovanni and tells him to eat first. She says his father once was a close friend of Campanella's father. Before he leaves for the festival she tells him not to go into the river, and she suggests closing the window because it is cooler now."},{"name":"ジョバンニの父","reading":"じょばんにのちち","category":"character","keys":["ジョバンニの父","お父さん","ジョバンニのお父さん"],"content":"Giovanni's father is away, and Giovanni believes he has been at sea fishing. Giovanni's mother fears he may not have gone out to sea. Giovanni insists he could not have done anything bad enough to be put in prison. He once gave the school a large crab shell and deer antlers, which are kept in the specimen room, and he promised Giovanni a sea otter jacket."},{"name":"マルソ","reading":"まるそ","category":"character","keys":["マルソ"],"content":"Maruso is a classmate who was with Giovanni and Campanella on the festival night. He runs up to Giovanni at the river and tells him that Campanella has fallen into the water. He explains that Zanelli fell from the boat while pushing a lantern, Campanella jumped in and pushed Zanelli toward the boat, and Campanella then could not be seen."},{"name":"カトウ","reading":"かとう","category":"character","keys":["カトウ"],"content":"Katō is a boy on the boat during the festival night who catches Zanelli after she falls into the river. He holds onto Zanelli until Zanelli is brought to the boat."},{"name":"カムパネルラのお父さん","reading":"かむぱねるらのおとうさん","category":"character","keys":["カムパネルラのお父さん","カムパネルラのお父さん"],"content":"Campanella's father is a doctor with a pointed, pale chin who was once a friend of Giovanni's father. When Campanella goes missing in the river, he stands among the townspeople and students, dressed in black and holding a watch, staring at the water. He is still waiting there while the others search for his son."},{"name":"ザウエル","reading":"ざうえる","category":"character","keys":["ザウエル"],"content":"Zauel is a dog whose tail looks like a broom. He follows Giovanni on his deliveries, sniffing and trotting along to the corner of the town, and sometimes farther. Giovanni says the dog will also follow the others when they go to float lanterns on the river that night."},{"name":"烏瓜のあかり","reading":"からすうりのあかり","category":"item","keys":["烏瓜のあかり","烏うり","烏瓜"],"content":"Lanterns made from kara-uri gourds that people float down the river during the Milky Way festival. Campanella and the others take them to the river that night. Zanelli is pushing one of these lanterns into the current from a boat when he falls into the water."}]}
